<section class="hero"><div class="wrap hero-layout"><div class="hero-emblem"><img src="images/cork-marine-deck-emblem.png" alt="Cork Marine Deck Specialists emblem" width="1536" height="1024" /></div><div class="hero-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Natural cork marine decking</span><h1>A Better Decking Experience. Naturally.</h1><p>Explore Jelinek AquaCork marine decking—a natural alternative designed for comfort, traction, and a distinctive finish on the water.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="#contact">Request a Decking Consultation</a><a class="button outline" href="#benefits">Explore Benefits</a></div></div></div></section>
<section id="aquacork" class="wrap section product-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Meet Jelinek AquaCork</span><h2>The natural upgrade your deck deserves.</h2><p class="lead">Beautiful marine decking should do more than look the part. AquaCork brings the character of natural cork to life aboard, combining a warm, distinctive finish with comfort underfoot and manufacturer-described non-skid performance.</p><p>From relaxed mornings on the aft deck to busy days around the cockpit, AquaCork offers a compelling alternative to conventional deck finishes. Its renewable cork origin, cushioning feel, and inviting texture make it worth considering for a thoughtful vessel refit.</p><a class="text-link" href="#contact">Explore AquaCork for your vessel →</a></div><aside class="product-highlight"><span>THE AQUACORK DIFFERENCE</span><strong>Natural beauty.<br />Purposeful performance.</strong><p>Warm underfoot · Distinctive texture · Marine-focused design</p></aside></section>
<section id="benefits" class="wrap section"><div class="center"><span class="eyebrow">Why AquaCork</span><h2>Comfort that belongs on the water.</h2><p>A thoughtfully selected marine decking material can change how your vessel looks and feels.</p></div><div class="grid">
<article><b>01 / COMFORT</b><h3>Comfort underfoot</h3><p>Cork's resilient character offers a welcoming surface for time spent aboard.</p></article>
<article><b>02 / TRACTION</b><h3>Designed for wet decks</h3><p>Jelinek describes AquaCork as a non-skid marine decking option. No surface is slip-proof.</p></article>
<article><b>03 / CLIMATE</b><h3>Thermal comfort</h3><p>Explore the manufacturer-described thermal benefits of cork in sunny marine environments.</p></article>
<article><b>04 / STYLE</b><h3>Natural warmth</h3><p>Warm cork tones bring a refined appearance to your vessel.</p></article>
<article><b>05 / QUIET</b><h3>Sound and vibration</h3><p>Cork is valued for sound- and vibration-dampening properties.</p></article>
<article><b>06 / MATERIAL</b><h3>Renewable cork</h3><p>Cork bark can be harvested without felling the cork oak tree.</p></article>
</div></section>
<section id="care" class="care section"><div class="wrap"><div class="center"><span class="eyebrow">Simple care, lasting appeal</span><h2>Enjoy the deck. Know how to care for it.</h2><p>AquaCork is designed for life on the water. A little attention to cleaning and surface protection helps keep your deck looking its best.</p></div><div class="care-grid"><article><span>01 / ROUTINE CLEANING</span><h3>Keep it looking fresh</h3><p>Remove dirt and debris regularly, and clean spills promptly. Use cleaning products and methods approved for your particular AquaCork finish; avoid aggressive chemicals or abrasive methods unless Jelinek confirms their suitability.</p></article><article><span>02 / STAIN RESISTANCE</span><h3>Ready for real boating life</h3><p>Properly sealed AquaCork is designed to resist everyday stains. Jelinek highlights resistance to challenging spills, including red wine and fish blood. Prompt cleanup and an intact sealer remain important; stain resistance does not mean stain-proof.</p></article><article><span>03 / SEALER MAINTENANCE</span><h3>Protect the finish annually</h3><p>Jelinek recommends annual sealer reapplication for optimal protection. Follow its current product-specific instructions, including surface preparation and drying requirements, before returning the deck to use.</p></article></div><p class="care-source">For detailed procedures and approved products, consult <a href="https://jelinek.com/install-maintenance-guides" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Jelinek’s installation and maintenance guidance</a>.</p></div></section>
<section id="process" class="dark section"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">Our approach</span><h2>Precision from planning to the final detail.</h2><p>Every vessel is different. Our proposed process puts careful assessment and manufacturer-approved installation requirements first.</p><div class="steps"><div><b>01</b><h3>Consult</h3><p>Discuss your goals.</p></div><div><b>02</b><h3>Measure</h3><p>Plan the layout.</p></div><div><b>03</b><h3>Prepare</h3><p>Evaluate the substrate.</p></div><div><b>04</b><h3>Install</h3><p>Follow approved methods.</p></div><div><b>05</b><h3>Review</h3><p>Discuss care and maintenance.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section id="applications" class="wrap section"><span class="eyebrow">Applications & inspiration</span><h2>Made for the places you enjoy most.</h2><p>Explore decking possibilities for cockpits, aft decks, swim platforms, walkways, and steps, subject to suitability.</p><div class="gallery"><div>Aft decks & cockpits</div><div>Swim platforms</div><div>Steps & walkways</div></div><p class="note">Design placeholders only. Genuine installation photography will be added with permission.</p></section>
<section class="wrap section"><span class="eyebrow">Product assurance</span><h2>Clear information. No guesswork.</h2><p class="assurance">Applicable AquaCork manufacturer warranty and care documentation will be provided once confirmed in writing by Jelinek. No specific warranty term or service-life guarantee is represented here.</p></section>
